{
  "schema_version": "1.7.0",
  "id": "USN-8839-1",
  "summary": "atril vulnerabilities",
  "details": "It was discovered that Atril did not properly sanitize command-line\narguments in PDF /GoToR actions. If a user opened a specially crafted PDF\nfile, an attacker could possibly use this issue to execute arbitrary code.\n(CVE-2026-46529)\n\nIt was discovered that Atril incorrectly handled certain PDF files. An\nattacker could possibly use this issue to cause a denial of service or\nto execute arbitrary code. This issue only affected Ubuntu 16.04 LTS.\n(CVE-2019-1010006)\n\nAndy Nguyen discovered that Atril incorrectly handled certain images. An\nattacker could possibly use this issue to expose sensitive information.\nThis issue only affected Ubuntu 16.04 LTS. (CVE-2019-11459)",
